R003 -> D003
added I014, I015, I016, I017; dropped none. The tip is E007: 0.7542 accuracy in 8.257 s at 9 epochs, only 0.12 pp above the 0.753 bar. Accuracy falls about 1 pp per epoch below 9 epochs, so trimming epochs is no longer possible without gaining accuracy first. The profile showed the step is GPU-bound in cuDNN and that conv kernel choice is already near-optimal, so the only systems lever left is a visible non-conv kernel. That is the new priority-4 idea: swap adaptive_max_pool2d for amax, because its atomic backward kernel takes ~2.5% of GPU time. I added two ideas that trade compute against accuracy: shrinking the last block to 512 (directly tests H1.5.1) and cutting block 1 to depth 2 (explore, H1.5). Each saves ~5-6% of FLOPs. I also added a schedule-shape idea (halve the warmup, decay to zero) to fill the gap D001 found, aiming to win back the margin needed to retry 8.5 epochs. I kept I012 (Muon at bs 1024, the main epoch-saving bet), I008 (progressive resizing) and I013 (proxy batch selection, explore). I006 (lookahead ablation) is still running. I dropped nothing: none of the queued ideas tests a settled hypothesis. The queue now has 7 queued ideas.
